# The module's own table, its words and settings. First: the other files will add to that table.
SpeedLeveling.lua
# A leveling guide written as text, read into our own shape; run for the character: where you are, what is done
Format.lua
Run.lua
# The guide shown: the known guide's while it is loaded, else one pasted as text; what its steps at hand want
Guide.lua
# What the key looks for around you, by name: your guide's step, your quests' objectives, the NPCs to hand in to;
# the things of the world your quests want, by ID
Wanted.lua
# What the key uses: the hearth when your guide's step wants it, else one quest item when nothing is found
Items.lua
# The key: loot, fight, talk or find, chosen by the game's secure ways at each press
Key.lua
# The guide over the world, and the window of the guides kept as text
Steps.lua
Guides.lua
